 "audit": "No cohort-wide novel finding is reported: the significant associations are overwhelmingly textbook (H3-3A, TP53, ATRX, DDX3X, CTNNB1, SMARCB1, BRAF, IDH1, PTCH1), and I did not manufacture ten 'new' findings. Candidates that may be less established: NOTCH2 in embryonal RMS, MED12 in ependymoma, NF2 in pilocytic astrocytoma (the last may reflect diagnosis mislabelling or NF2-associated cases), so treat them as hypotheses. 21 hypermutated cases (>100 mutated genes, up to 9075; mostly malignant glioma) created many spurious passenger-gene 'associations' and were excluded. Diagnosis labels are heterogeneous (NOS, missing, Unknown, overlapping glioma terms), cohort is mixed-center, case-mix is unbalanced, 128 cases have no mutations, only exome data, no copy-number/fusions, and tests are multiple (~214 after filtering) though q-values are small for reported claims. Control group is all other tumors, so associations reflect comparison with a mixed background.",
 "methods": "Per-case gene-level mutation presence; excluded 21 hypermutators (>100 genes). For each diagnosis with n>=8 (excluding missing/Unknown) and gene mutated in >=3 cases with higher frequency than the rest, two-sided Fisher exact test versus all other cases, Benjamini-Hochberg across tests. Reported claims at q<~1e-3 with biological plausibility, probabilities discounted for small counts and label heterogeneity; frequencies are observed fractions."
